Subject: [PATCH 02530/11362] [conductor] Pre-gate block: PHASE A2 (HEADLINE
 skeptic-proofing; GATED on exp4381 detector_localization_actionable==true) --
 is the A1 localization/abstention win GENUINE, or an artifact? The operator
 (twice-burned on over-claims) will ask: does the bidirectional localization
 win come from (a) POSITION/LENGTH bias (the detector just predicts 'the error
 is late/early' -- test against a position-only baseline that ignores
 content), (b) R2L FUTURE-CONTEXT LEAK making the bidirectional gain
 ONLINE-INVALID (the bidirectional number uses suffix context an in-loop actor
 never has -- confirm the causal/L2R-only delta is the honest online claim),
 or (c) single-split/seed OVERFIT (re-test on a held-out split + a second seed
 regime, bootstrap CI95)? This DIAGNOSTIC (no new scoring infra, no live LLM)
 re-tests the A1 winning localization three ways and decides whether the
 actionable-detector headline graduates. Emit localization_win_is_genuine BARE
 bool := (the A1 localization advantage survives the position-only-baseline
 control AND the causal-online delta is itself > 0 with CI95-excl-0 AND it
 holds on a held-out split). verifier_is_oracle=false. A pass = the
 actionable-detector headline graduates; a fail = the A1 win is
 artifact-confounded and is QUARANTINED + the residual logged as a
 missing-verifier gap. NO TRM training; CPU-offline.

1 of 1 gate(s) failed; first failure: exp4381-biprm-detector-localization-abstention.detector_localization_actionable (actual=False == expected=True)

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
